{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":43824,"duration_api_ms":43775,"num_turns":14,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"af09d3a3-a938-49ce-b0ba-ffdeb2e2d64c","total_cost_usd":0.327556,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26920,"cache_read_input_tokens":221882,"output_tokens":1933,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26920,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1933,"cacheReadInputTokens":221882,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26920,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.327556,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Both amendments verified against source code. Amendment fr-5-d6a4b57a: concentration_from_total() at nitrogen_cycle.rs:383-389 is byte-for-byte identical to concentration() at water.rs:301-307 — a clear DRY violation with divergence risk. Amendment fr-5-4a64f0c3: algae_growth.rs directly calls state.water.tan_mg_n_per_l(volume_l) bypassing the ConcentrationView abstraction used everywhere else. Both are low-risk, mechanical refactors that improve consistency and maintainability.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-d6a4b57a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: concentration_from_total() in nitrogen_cycle.rs (lines 383-389) is character-for-character identical to the private concentration() function in water.rs (lines 301-307). Both check is_finite() on total and volume_l, guard volume_l <= f64::EPSILON, and clamp with .max(0.0). This is a textbook DRY violation — if the safety logic evolves (e.g., adding subnormal handling or logging), only one copy gets updated. Extracting to a single pub(crate) function is straightforward and eliminates silent divergence risk."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-4a64f0c3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: algae_growth.rs is the sole system file that calls state.water.tan_mg_n_per_l(volume_l) directly (line 14), computing volume_l separately at line 10. Every other consumer — plant_growth.rs, shrimp.rs, events.rs, snapshot.rs — uses state.concentrations() which internally calls water_volume_l() to get volume. The ConcentrationView abstraction exists precisely to centralize the volume computation and provide a uniform API. Standardizing algae_growth.rs to use it reduces coupling to WaterState internals, ensures volume is always computed through the canonical path, and makes the codebase consistently follow the same pattern. The change is mechanical (replace three direct calls with one concentrations() call and field access)."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0a14c190-aec6-482c-b44d-75a141d2e763"}
